Z||000016||Tigger||12-05-2000||09:24 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fformula88:<BR><B>Just a side note on GM execs driving new GM cars:<P>GM decided that there wasn't enough Aztecs running around Michigan and figured one way to bolster the image and attract buyers was to have more of them out and about on the highways.  (They never thought to make it look good I guess  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> )  So, they have made 2000 of their execs turn in their GM exec cars and take Aztecs.  They are supposed to drive them around and look like they are having fun and enjoying them!  Poor guys, but I guess its what they deserve for putting out such a POS!!!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>LOL, that is sooo true, I've been fortunate to see them all summer long, even before they were on sale.  Eh hem, there are a few of them parked in a lot just outside, shhhh.  From the stories I've heard, the Aztek is really a nice "vehicle" on the inside.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>If I owned GM, hmmm... I would move everything south so I could enjoy nice weather all year long.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Today we had our first 1" of snow on the roads, they were smacking them up pretty good on the morning drive.<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000017||DrRodey||12-05-2000||11:44 AM||||I know this entire post was just for fun.. but here's my .02    <P>I have found that one of the biggest drawing points to the wonderful world of Fieros is that they are the ONLY mid engine two seat US car.  Not only that but they are fun as hell to customise.  Most of the options y'all wanna put on your 'new' Fiero you already have modified into your current ones.  I don't think what we need to do is Buy GM and restart the Fiero line... what needs to be done is The construction of a special factory making all the replacement/custom parts that are not available anymore.  They could also take design requests for custom body work ect..  <P>I think that would be a much better place for out time and money to go. It would be to the good of the Fiero to keep it in it's own little nitch in history.  Not to start over from scratch. <P>Thanks for the space.||||reg||1
Z||000018||frontal lobe||12-05-2000||02:09 PM||||OK Bam-Bam, I'm in.  But with about 1600 members on the forum we would have to get about half the members committed.  And reading the posts over the last year, probably about half of the members SHOULD be committed (joke).<P>If I was one of the couple thousand of people who had to drive an Aztek, in protest I would put a bag over my head when driving it.<P>You know, when people start talking about how nice the INTERIOR of a car is, it's like people telling you what a GREAT PERSONALITY your blind date has...||||reg||1
