Z||000025||Will||12-05-2000||06:35 PM||||Azteks: There was a career fair here at VT earlier this semester and GM had a coupel of cars there (a C5-R and a Z06  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> I got to sit in it as they drove it back to the trailer that afternoon  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>     Anyway, two of the guys had an Aztek to drive around in (the guy who drove the Corvette heritage tractor trailer had the Z06.. poor unfortunate slob). He said its like a girl who's so ugly you wouldn't touch her with a 10 foot pole but who's so nice you start to like her anyway...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"> for whatever that's worth.<P>     What's the most unreplaceable part on the Fiero? also the most common since it's on every one? and is not being produced by ANYONE anymore? The only part EVERY Fiero enthusiast likes, without exception?<P>The space frame.<P>NEW PRODUCT: a tubular aluminum space frame with honeycombed aluminum panels epoxied in; more torsional stiffness than a Ferrari 360; 250 lbs lighter than the original; the same mounting points as the original so that ALL Fiero OEM body panels, interior parts, suspension bits, cradles, etc. bolt up to it without modification; red powder coated finish available in your choice of colors!<P>You were going to buy a body kit and interior kit anyway, right? Now you don't have to worry about disposing of the old body parts and interior! You don't have to strip a donor car either! Half your problem is solved!<P>Also available in PLUS SIZES for those of you who just can't make due with a transverse powertrain and feel the need a longitudinal big block!<P>Call for pricing. Call your bank and secure a line of credit first.<P>On a more serious (?) note, count me in on the fund thing. I would like a say in GM's direction.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000026||DaRkLoRD||12-05-2000||07:01 PM||||Seriously, with enough capital invested from several different car groups, it should be possible to start a totally new car company... first product would be a modern Fiero.. but we could make other cars with similar designs, and they'd be just as light, strong, efficient, etc..<P>a friend at college mentioned to me that he applied for a grant, and received $40,000.... if several of us do that, and then pool the resources, we'd have a serious shot at making a small company.. if we cater to more than one market, the revenue could grow fairly fast.. Look st Saleen for example, he worked with Mustangs for years, and this year he designed his own car from scratch.. there's a lot of diverse knowledge on the forum, and I bet a lot of young engineers, designers, etc would jump at the chance to work at a new car company.. especially they see some of the prototypes.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>unless you guys are *all* joking, in which case, let me confess that I tend to take things literally... hehe<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||3
