Z||000031||BAM-BAM||12-05-2000||10:05 PM||||  I kind of like the idea of buying the rights to the Fiero. After all the effort that GM has put forth to divorce themselves from our plastic friend, I wouldn't think they would'nt ask to much. Let them keep the rights to the power plant, and we'll take all else. From this point we can negotiate with reputable vendors to implement Certain modernizations on such things as the interior ergonomics, exterior scoops and panel inprovements, braking system upgrades,<BR>and overall suspension design and/or enhancement. As for the power train, we have enough braniacs here to design and construct an awesome V6, tranverse mounted power plant, coupled a 6-speed autostick. Lighten the over all waight of the vehical by about three hundred pounds with a base HP of around 270HP and over 300# of torque. These are things that are only out of the reach of the ney-sayers. All models will be peak performance based with the only options being in the exterior and interior cosmetics.<BR> Each vehical will be manufactured in it's entirety in North America and with parts and systems designed and built in North America. There will be no Foreign influence alowed in the design constuction or implimentation of "OUR" vehical with the exception of the electrical systems and gauges designed by a European firm <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P>  Come on guys/gals, this is the opportunity of a lifetime. Bigger things have started with smaller ideas than this, and grown to monumental success (Microsoft). What it takes is a belief, in the end result of the culmination of the ideas and desires of the people of this forum. "You" have the power to change the future of all of Fierodom. Those of you who say that, "what makes the Fiero so special is it's limited production", can stay on the couch. Those who believe that the Fiero was cut down in it's prime, step forward, let's pick up the pieces and let the dream run it's course to fruition. The Fiero was and remains, a victim of corperate and social cynicism. To "HELL" with the Corvette! The Fiero should have been and will be the "Flagship" of american muscle. It's time to take our proper place. It's time for "YOU" to make a difference.<P>  Peace, B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT<BR>Eibach/KYB Susp.<BR>Mr.Mikes 500 series seats,headliner! MOMO Commando Steering Wheel, White Face Race Style Gauges And Soon To Be More!!! YEAH BABY-YEAH||||reg||12
Z||000032||MikeE||12-06-2000||01:05 AM||||I agree with Will.  We need to find a way to save the Fieros that are left.  Many will bite the dust when their frames rust out and so far, no one is making a complete or partial replacement.  In addition, many Fieros with good frames meet the crusher, at least here in Hawaii, and they should be saved.<P>Before we think about a new car, we need to find manufacturers for the pieces we need for our cars.  For instance, I wish GM or someone would make a decent transverse manual trans rated at more than 200 lb-ft of torque so we could have a reliable trans for the engines we all want in our cars.  Replacement tubular control arms would be nice, and so on...<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
