Z||000035||Will||12-06-2000||01:01 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MikeE:<BR><B>I agree with Will.  We need to find a way to save the Fieros that are left.  Many will bite the dust when their frames rust out and so far, no one is making a complete or partial replacement.  In addition, many Fieros with good frames meet the crusher, at least here in Hawaii, and they should be saved.<P>Before we think about a new car, we need to find manufacturers for the pieces we need for our cars.  For instance, I wish GM or someone would make a decent transverse manual trans rated at more than 200 lb-ft of torque so we could have a reliable trans for the engines we all want in our cars.  Replacement tubular control arms would be nice, and so on...<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The Volkswagen 02A transaxle, while not even strong enough stock for a 3.4 has several 6 speed kits available for it, good for 300 ft lbs all the way to 400++ ft lbs. An outfit in Britain <A HREF="http://www.stealthracing.co.uk" TARGET=_blank>http://www.stealthracing.co.uk</A>  makes the kit that EIP tuning uses behind their 500+ HP turbo VR6 engines.<BR>Problem: the kit costs 2600 pounds, and the exchange rate sucks.||||reg||1
