Z||000046||BAM-BAM||12-07-2000||10:54 PM||||  Ok, Let's get the ball rolling on the PFF/GM take over. For starters, there has to be someone here that knows of a good investment attourney. I would look around Vegas, but that would yeild as much as looking for a virgin in a brothel. Lot of unmotivated ambulance chasers here. Or perhaps there is someone on the Forum that knows the in's and out's of Group investing. Option three, I could look into what it takes to start an investment group, other than the capitol resources.  I believe that should be phase I. I will entertain any brainstorming. Phase II will be to pull together the investors and the neccessary contractual forms to make this leagal. Also the need exists to form a group name. One idea would be to restructure periodicaly under a new name to throw GM off track. Don't want them to get the idea that there are people out here interested in relieving them of there "burden". Phase III, sit and wait. Watch the capitol grow and keep a close eye on what GM is doing. During this period it would be advantageous to make relative decisions on future corporate structuring. Getting our ducks in a row. This is not going to happen over night, so be patient. It might also be wise to look into diversification and locate some high yield bonds and CD's to further grow the capitol fund. Set the benchmark at where it seems probable that our efforts will be maximised. All it takes is one or two or even three member of our group to occupy a board seat. At that point the decision making proccess becomes increasingly influenced by "US". With the proper management these funds can grow exponentialy in relatively short order (not overnight). Patients is the key phrase here. <P>Let's start a correspondence within the group to see exactly how feasible this really is. It can't be done with just a few. In an endeavor like this it requires the power of numbers. We need people who believe in this effort to see it to fruition. Who' in, let's see a show of hands.<P> Peace, B2 OUT!  <P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT<BR>Eibach/KYB Susp.<BR>Mr.Mikes 500 series seats,headliner! MOMO Commando Steering Wheel, White Face Race Style Gauges And Soon To Be More!!! YEAH BABY-YEAH||||reg||12
