Z||000059||BAM-BAM||12-10-2000||08:32 PM||||   At that point you would have to use Government buisness loans or open yourself up to outside investors. I really don't like the idea of outsiders coming in. <BR>  The idea about the fiberglass panels is sound. I like that, they are easier to work with and modify. <BR>  A limited production of say, 10 vehicals, of varrying options, ie...T-top GT, Targa top GT, or perhaps even a Convertable GT. I am not inclined to go with a coupe design. This is supposed to be a muscle car. Remember the power plant and drive train are the same, only the exterior elevation and interior ergonomics are optional and limited at that. It will have to be an affordable alternative to todays overpriced under powered "Sports Cars". We have to produce the "Most Bang Fot The Buck". <BR>  Perhaps another alternative (Still in line with buying the rights to the Fiero) Would be to buy the rights make the changes and the limited production models, then turn around and sell the venture back to GM with a "production Royalty Guaranty" and a guarantied production clause. This clause will ensure that X amount are produced and that the investment group receives royalties on the production numbers with a minimum figure guarantied. That's just a thought.<BR>  I would rather get the rights produce a few, check market demands and mortgage the house, sell the farm, cash in the old 401K because that will all be a pittence comparably.<P> What do you all think? LMK<P> Peace, B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  ||||reg||12
