Z||000062||BAM-BAM||12-11-2000||12:38 AM||||  Steve, lets look at it like this; with the first production run of test vehicals, you could virtually build them in your garage. Most of the design and implimentation is done in an office or outsourced to vendors. Once all of the "test" products are in place, it's a small task to put the kit together. Then of course there would have to be the safety vehical sent to test for concurrent safety acceptance. This would include upgraded safety fetures such as, dual airbags (not Clinton-Gore) Side impact airbags or improved side impact structure, 4<BR>wheel ABS, signal mirrors, auto dimming mirros, the all new wide track stance and better lighting and alumination. Once it is accepted for safety and emissions there will be the normal road testing, cross country, duration and reliability. Of course with Navstar, or Onstar, this will be the  envy of the sport car world. After all applicable testing, we can set forth on the marketing end of things. Announce the "New Breed" in all the big car mags, bulletin boards, and infomercials to check how the public responds. Once there is public acceptance, and there will be, We will be able to finance a small limited production facility. As the company grows, so does the facility, which by the way, is constructed in such a manner to alow for rapid and cost effective expansion. <BR>  This is a very feasable idea that will take some serious planning, starting with the aquisition of the Fiero from GM. From there, our local gearheads can brainstorm with various vendors to produce the neccessary changes to derive at our new and improved model. Then it's just a matter of time. <BR>  We are the people who drive these cars every day. No one knows better than we do, collectively, what to do to make this the "new breed" of the millenium. No one knows better than we, what it would take to sell us on this new product. We are a good crossection of the world we live in. It's the everyday person that knows what it takes to please the everyday person. We are everyday people. <BR>  This is the vision; A sports car that is pound for pound, the best "VALUE" on the market. Complete with the latest in technology and engineering, but no to far removed from it's roots. Mid engine, two seats, and more fun than the average person should be alowed to have. Completely safe from road to roof. 0-60 in 6 or better, quarter time in the 12's, Fiero, there is no substitute. Interior comfort beyond compare, digital gauges(Cliff), leather seatin and panels, real carbon fiber trim color matched, Latest in stereophonic detail, and the list goes on. Well set on stock 18's with a nice wide footprint. Lets not forget the sound of that exhaust, no one else will.<BR>  This is a glimpse of the possibilities and I'm just one person. There are those of you on this forum that have the know how to bring out the details in all that I have put before you. Feel free, this is "OUR" endeavor. Hell If I had the capitol, I  would have this thing going tomorrow. I don't, so maybe we can. Every great corporation started with one mans small idea and big dreams. This is much a probability as was Microsoft or General Motors, Ford and the rest. <BR>  I will write to General Motors, Pontiac division and inquire about the sale of the rights to the Fiero. When I get a response I will post it here, the only place that needs to know. I am serious and to show that, I will start the ball rolling. But, Once it starts, Y'all be ready to jump before it rolls on by.<P> Peace, B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">      ||||reg||12
Z||000063||Cheever2||12-11-2000||12:48 AM||||Mine eyes have seen the coming of the glory...<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000064||DaRkLoRD||12-11-2000||02:11 AM||||Sounds like a good plan, and if it'd work... sign me up for whatever I'm needed to do.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>the only concern I have, is how much GM would want for the Fiero design.. it would surprise me if they asked for anything less than a million dollars, assuming they were willing to sell at all. If they're not willing to sell the design, we could still build our own, using the same ideas as above. Personally that's what I'd rather do, as it would free up money that would otherwise just be going to GM execs..<P>but I'm more than willing to help, no matter what path is taken for this..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||3
