Z||000075||LuckyTheyWereEverMade||12-16-2000||04:53 AM||||Ummmm . . . Once question, fellow Fierophiles, Did any of you see the election this year.  Ballots and elections only work well when the count is decisive.  Imagine going to court to review all the close decisions.  Right now were all friends with a common interest.  I hate to quote Cindy Lauper, but "Money Changes Everything."<BR>Enjoy your cars for as long as you can make them last.  Fill your garage and yard with parts cars.  Spend all your money on those factory "super duty" parts before their gone.  All good things must ultimately come to an end.  Until then, laugh at those stupid tiny little electric and electric/hybrid vehicles like the prius and insight.  On the topic of an aftermarket space frame, why aren't we dreaming of carbon fiber?  Go bicycle shopping and you will find that Aluminum is not so "chic" anymore.  Alcoa is aluminum cans.  Carbon Fiber is higher tech than the space shuttle.  For that matter so is a 286 PC computer.  Think about it and enjoy what you have now.  After all, you could be driving a Kia!||||reg||4
